Whether the Hamiltonian reading is the right classical limit of the record's amplitude for a long-range gate, given that:
- its kinematic and canonical velocities decouple (sigma_kin/sigma_c up to 11.5 in the N-body);
- its linear theory leaves the interpretable regime at eps >~ 2.24-2.29 (critic3/c4 (c)).

new_gaps.why_it_matters:
It has the shape of Paul's question. Any 'no carrier' statement given to Paul needs this caveat and its limits:
- the threshold rho v r ~ 1 depends on distance;
- no tensor version exists;
- the record contains no such field.

